    {
      "platform": "windows",
      "version": "3.12.2",
      "release_date": "2026-11-16",
      "release_notes": "- Windows installer: Italian and Spanish translations and file properties #562\n- Windows: default silent install and uninstall to the current user when no install mode is specified #561\n- Windows: rebuild launcher to avoid concatenation in the installer, hopefully flagging less virus heuristics #565\n- Enable Comments fetcher by default for new users\n- Fix loading of results exported from other feeders than IP Range #387\n- Open dialogs on the same monitor as the main window, even if it is above or to the left of the primary one #346\n- Do not restore the main window outside of the visible area, e.g. after disconnecting an external screen #393\n- Show comments stored by MAC address regardless of the order of columns #419\n- Windows: pass IPv4 addresses to ICMP and ARP APIs as plain integers, which may fix bogus alive hosts and MAC addresses #337 #395 #488\n- Fix reverse IP ranges (start > end) scanning past the end when crossing a byte boundary\n- IP List File feeder: detect the network interface for all hosts, not only the first one\n- Linux: fix leaking of file descriptors when reading the ARP table\n- TCP pinger: fix possible hanging after a very fast reply and keep probing the port that has responded\n- UDP pinger: count actual UDP replies as alive\n- Hostname fetcher: accept hostnames that resolve to multiple addresses, e.g. both IPv4 and IPv6\n- Do not use 100% of a CPU core while waiting for a free thread if thread delay is 0\n- Updated translations for all languages",
      "release_notes_url": "https://github.com/angryip/ipscan/releases/tag/3.12.2",
      "manifest_version": "1.28.0",
